	"title": "no interleaving: a splice by ids also names the element it goes before at its writer (WIRE.md, ids), and inserts at one place go by FugueMax's rule, so two devices typing at one place keep their words whole in any direction: each prepending a word a character at a time (abc, xyz), each typing backward in the middle, each adding three todos at the top of a list, and each typing forward, come out one word then the other on every peer, whatever came first. old steps, ids with no before, go as they did (before them: the end), so two old prepends still mix. before as an id, as true (its after's) and none decode; true with no after, or a fourth item, is not a step (its steps' bytes here, before and all)",
